th to join a chess club at a high  school every Thursday he wants her to  play everyone simultaneously since there  are rarely girls playing chess this  would be a great opportunity for both  Beth and the orphanage the warden thinks  about it for a while and approves it  much to the Delight of Mr gonze  afterwards Beth goes to get her vitamin  doses but learns that the orphanage has  changed their pills this worries her as  she has become addicted to the pills in  a sign of desperation she approaches  Jolene to ask for some of hers but the  latter tells her that she's only having  withdrawal symptoms the next day Beth  heads to the chess club but she isn't in  a good mood because of the absence of  the pills that she so depends on but  fortunately as she is about to leave  Jolene gives her a couple of pills and  wishes her good luck shortly after Beth  reaches the high school where a group of  Chess playing boys are present they are  surprised to see a girl and keep staring  at her dude put down the pawns is that a  female we learn that Beth has to play  all of the boys at once this is likely  the kinkiest thing these boys will ever  do as she takes them all on a crowd of  students gathers they are eager to  witness the girl getting humiliated  however to everyone's shock Beth  outplays every single opponent and ends  all the matches inside an hour and 20  minutes later she proudly tells Mr  chibel what happened despite her  Brilliance Beth's dependence on vitamin  pills forces her to act desperately  during a movie night she pretends to go  to the bathroom but breaks into the  orphanage Pharmacy she then starts  stealing pills and gobbles them up like  candy after a while she grabs the entire  pill jar and heads out Beth wants to  hide it in her room but unfortunately  before she can move she collapses due to  vitamin overdose the teachers and  students arrive at the same time and  catch her in the act in the next scene  Beth is being punished for stealing the  vitamin pills from today on she is  forbidden to practice Chess at the high  school upset she approaches Mr chibel  and informs him about the punishment she  then wishes to continue playing chess  with him as the years pass Jolene and  Beth become close friends they're now  the eldest in the orphanage one morning  Jolene reaches for a cigarette and heads  to the balcony as Beth gets up from bed  she joins Jolene and both of them spot a  car entering the orphanage grounds a  couple whom we know as Mr and Mrs  Whitley has come to adopt a child later  the warden calls every single student to  her office and the whitleys interview  them at last it's Beth's turn and she  manages to Captivate them with her  beauty and charm once the interview is  over she is asked to pack her belongings  Beth is officially adopted this takes  her over the moon but she is also sad  because she won't be playing with Mr  chibel again later Beth arrives at her  new house and the whitleys show her  around when they take her to her room  Beth is astounded by how much space she  will have for herself the next day she  wakes up to the wheatleys having an  argument about work-related matters Mr  Wheatley is about to leave on a business  trip and will be gone for two weeks we  learned that the couple isn't happy with  their marriage Beth heads off for her  first day of school and starts her life  as a normal teenager not surprisingly  she doesn't fit in with the kinds of  girls within the school most of them  make fun of her poor choice of clothes  to make matters worse Beth finds out  that there is no chess club in this  school the next day Mrs Wheatley takes  Beth to get some new clothes there she  sees some chess sets but Mrs Wheatley  refuses to buy her one as they are short  on money instead she wants Beth to start  saving bit by bit from her 40 cents  allowance so that she can buy one for  herself one day Mrs Wheatley asks Beth  to get her some packs of cigar threats  from the local convenience store  obliging to the request Beth heads out  and retrieves the cigarettes but as she  is about to leave the store she sees a  magazine related to chess however the  store owner doesn't let her read it for  free she needs to buy it Beth obviously  has no money so she steals the magazine  once home Mrs Wheatley mentions that  there isn't enough money to run the  house until the end of the month they  only get 70 dollars from her husband  Which is far less than they need how did  these people pass the adoption exam  hearing her worries Beth comes up with  an idea she wants to take part in the  chess competition the winner of which  will receive 100 there is a small catch  though the entry fee is five dollars  bath requests Mrs Wheatley to lend her  some cash but the latter straight away  refuses left with no choice Beth writes  a letter to Mr scheibel asking for five  dollars to enter the chess tournament  she also mentions that she will pay him  back double the amount when she wins the  tournament as she is about to send the  letter Mrs Wheatley asks her to run out  for another errand this time it is for a  prescription once again obliges and when  she gets the pills she realizes that  they are the same ones that the  orphanage used to provide later Mrs  Wheatley mentions that it is her  Tranquility medicine Beth hands her the  pill bottle but it is only half full as  she had already taken the other half for  herself now that she is reunited with  her vitamin pills Beth again begins to  practice chess on the ceiling the next  day she gets a letter from Mr chibel as  expected he has sent her the five  dollars with this Beth immediately  enters the chess tournament but when she  reaches the venue the organizers tell  her that there's no women's section they  also make fun of her and tell her to go  away however Beth is determined and she  asserts that there is no law that states  a girl cannot play chess because of the  rant the organizers reluctantly set her  up on The Beginner's list Beth's first  opponent is a girl and she defeats her  quickly afterwards she watches state  champions play each other in the second  round Beth beats her opponent and even  forces him to resign before ending the  day she has to play against a boy named  towns he is a Charming Man so Beth keeps  on Staring at him during the game  however this doesn't distract her from  the game and she easily beats him  despite the defeat towns is genuinely  impressed with how good she is for her  age when she returns home Beth finds Mrs  wheatley's room turned into a rack  apparently her husband left her and only  informed her over the phone the next day  Beth returns to the tournament to face  her last opponent Harry beltick the  state champion we learned that Harry has  arrogance about him he is so sure that  he will win the finals that he arrives  late to the tournament after the game  commences Harry immediately gets on the  front foot by displaying some impressive  moves feeling the pressure Beth heads to  the bathroom and Pops a pill to ease her  nerves she then returns with more  confidence and puts up a good fight at  last she eventually beats Harry and wins  the whole tournament because of this  Beth becomes a sensation in the local  papers of Kentucky she wins a hundred  dollars and heads home with the check  this Delights Mrs Wheatley and she  finally starts to acknowledge Beth's  skills it turns out that she didn't know  the game could pay so much the following  day miss this is Wheatley conducts an  Ardent and learns that a chess  tournament with prize money of 500 is  going to commence soon in Cincinnati she  informs Beth about it but the latter is  worried that she will miss school  fortunately Mrs Wheatley takes care of  this by lying to the principal that her  daughter is sick with this Beth agrees  to participate in the chess tournament  she then confidently asserts that she  will win the next morning we see Beth  and her mother arriving in Cincinnati  for the state tournament even here she  is well known by all the people they  call her the female genius wow even the  compliments are misogynistic her first  opponent is a nervous player who knows  her well before a game even starts he  admits defeat and wishes her good luck  what was that guy even doing here the  organizers from the earlier tournament  also show up to support Beth as they  have now become her number one fan they  have a discussion about participating in  the U.S open after that they talk about  the idea of playing in a Russian  tournament however they are skeptical  because it is believed that the Russians  are way better than the Americans at  chess in the next scene Beth wins this  Cincinnati tournament and gives her  mother 15 percent of the prize money as  a commission as time passes she goes on  to win various other tournaments around  the U.S our chess Prodigy is now more  and more popular and she draws attention  she is even interviewed by journalists  in her field in an interview Beth  reveals that she discovered chess in the  basement of her orphanage she also  explains that a janitor named Mr chibel  showed her some moves Beth also adds  that her great ability in chess comes  from the fact that she can predict how a  game will evolve and therefore play the  right way in order to win three years  pass and we see bath arriving in Las  Vegas in 1966 she is now a prosperous  woman who has the world at her feet  there she meets towns the Charming  opponent she met in Cincinnati towns is  now working as a magazine reporter and  he is here to write reviews on the chess  tournament he wishes to write an article  about bath and invites her to his room  to snap some photos for the paper Beth  agrees to follow him on the condition  that they play chess after the work is  finished God chess is so hot right now  once they arrive it is evident that  there is some chemistry between them  they are almost about to kiss but  unfortunately Town's roommate arrives  and ruins the moment in the next scene  Beth returns to her hotel room and finds  her mother drinking grabbing a bottle  herself Beth talks about her tournament  including her nervousness towards U.S  Champion Benny Watts he always has a  crowd around him and certainly knows how  to play later that day Beth runs into  Benny himself who discusses game  strategy the U.S Champion points out an  error that Beth made a few years ago he  explains that the previous player she  faced could have beaten her this  Revelation certainly rattles bath and  the most annoying thing is the fact that  Benny deduced her errors simply by  reading the report of the game the  following day Beth has to play the final  game with Benny although she manages to  keep a cool demeanor she begins to panic  eventually leading to her first ever  loss Beth is upset about her incapacity  to foresee what her opponent wanted to  do despite this she still gets a share  of the prize money just before Beth and  her mother leave Las Vegas towns rushes  after her and states that she'll have  another chance to face Benny in the  future the moral of the story is if you  want to be great at a game to see what  happens next watch the second part in  series recapped
 

